NOTES\P1. Chainstays 22.2 x 0.9 crimped to 16 x 27 oval from BB to 110 mm behind BB (clears 35 mm tyre AND 60T belt ring at 50 chainline).\P2. Stays run at 70.5 mm from centre plane near the dropout so the belt and rear cog clear the drive-side stays
  3
.\P3. Belt drive requires a frame split: bolted splitter in the drive-side seat stay (shown), or a split dropout per builder's standard.\P4. Sliding dropouts tension the belt and carry the rear post mount, 160 mm rotor (on the non-drive slider); 160 
  1
rotor on the non-drive side. Rotor and caliper clear the frame by >= 3 mm over the full travel. No rim-brake bridge.\P5. Rear hose: internal through top tube (6 mm ports, non-drive side), then along the non-drive seat stay on 2 x M4 guide bosses.
